2. Clean-Room Implementations, Academic Citations, and Differential References
================================================================================

- Trust-Region Bayesian Optimization (TuRBO):
  baux's trust-region optimizer (`TurboTrustRegion`) and its specification
  fixtures (`research/turbo_upstream.py`,
  `rust/crates/baux/src/trust_region/fixtures.toml`) are an independent
  clean-room implementation of the mathematical algorithm published in David
  Eriksson, Michael Pearce, Jacob R. Gardner, Ryan Turner, and Matthias
  Poloczek, "Scalable Global Optimization via Local Bayesian Optimization",
  NeurIPS 2019 (arXiv:1910.01739, Section 2), together with MIT-licensed
  BoTorch (`https://github.com/pytorch/botorch`) and `yubo-research/enn`. No
  source code, outputs, or artifacts from `uber-research/TuRBO` are incorporated
  or distributed.

- Manifold-Constrained Hyper-Connections (mHC):
  baux's Sinkhorn-Knopp Birkhoff polytope manifold projection (`fbt::moe`) is
  an independent Rust and Apple Silicon Metal implementation of Zhenda Xie et
  al., "mHC: Manifold-Constrained Hyper-Connections", arXiv:2512.24880 (2025),
  verified against `https://github.com/tokenbender/mHC-manifold-constrained-hyper-connections`
  (commit `ad20d0d8db4d6fc7e8d9b148281167141da20d47`, Apache-2.0 License).

- Tokamak Magnetic Control and Plasma Transport (WPO / Acme, TORAX, TokaGym):
  - baux's resident Rust and Metal tokamak control benchmark (`baux::tokamak`,
    `tokamak_policy.metal`) is a clean-room mathematical implementation of the
    WPO Table 6 (`shape_70166` Precise) 5-component reward and coupled dynamics
    from Brendan D. Tracey et al., "Towards practical reinforcement learning for
    tokamak magnetic control", Fusion Engineering and Design 200 (2024) 114161,
    and DeepMind Acme (`https://github.com/google-deepmind/acme`, commit
    `2e09e3ddecf4a1ba783688c92aa493c596a2beec`, Apache-2.0 License).
  - Optional external transport PDE coupling (`benchmarks/torax/`) interfaces
    with Google DeepMind TORAX (`https://github.com/google-deepmind/torax`,
    version 2.0.0, Apache-2.0 License; Jonathan Citrin et al., "TORAX: A Fast
    and Differentiable Tokamak Transport Simulator in JAX", arXiv:2406.06718).
  - Optional external TCV rampdown rollout evaluation (`benchmarks/tokagym/`)
    interfaces with EPFL/MIT TokaGym + contrax (Zenodo DOI
    `10.5281/zenodo.16621120`, MIT License; Allen M. Wang et al., Nature
    Communications 16 (2025) 8877; Christian Theiler et al., Nuclear Fusion 66
    (2026) 116007).

- Full-Weight Perturbation and Evolutionary Optimization Interfaces:
  The modular full-weight perturbation interface was independently implemented
  after studying Modular CMA-ES (MIT), IOHexperimenter (BSD-3-Clause),
  fcmaes-rust (MIT), Nevergrad (MIT), evosax (Apache-2.0), and EvoX (GPL-3.0).
  No source code from these projects is incorporated. EvoX is a research
  reference only; no GPL-covered implementation is included.

